WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.240
A muscle substance released in response to cold temperatures delayed aging markers and worms. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 221. After that, NAD Plus and Chromatin, light gated proteins that quiet heart cells, and a venomous primate gone from the records for decades. Experiments compared worms held at reduced temperatures with animals kept at standard conditions, as reported by Chosun. The muscle derived signal appeared only under cold and then influenced distant tissues.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.580
those tissues preserved function over time. Environmental temperature can modulate

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:40.200
aging processes through specific molecular signals. Work continues to identify the substance

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:46.214
and test its activity in other systems. Earlier temperature studies in flies and mice already

00:00:46.214 --> 00:00:51.314
showed lifespan extension under mild cold. If the substance or its human counterpart

00:00:51.314 --> 00:00:56.494
can be identified and measured, it could serve as a circulating biomarker for cold-induced

00:00:56.494 --> 00:01:01.334
protective states. Researchers will next need to determine whether the factor acts through

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:08.254
known longevity pathways, such as AMPK or MTOR, or through an independent route. The immediate

00:01:08.254 --> 00:01:12.694
experimental question is whether delivering the substance without lowering body temperature

00:01:12.694 --> 00:01:18.394
reproduces the aging delay. Identification of the molecule would allow direct tests in

00:01:18.394 --> 00:01:23.634
mammalian models to see whether the same pathway influences tissue maintenance or metabolic health.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:28.934
Analogous signals could then be measured in blood or muscle after controlled cold exposure

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.014
in larger animals.

00:01:30.983 --> 00:01:35.263
Most people assume that any benefit from cooler temperatures comes from reduced metabolic

00:01:35.263 --> 00:01:40.863
rate or simple calorie conservation, yet these experiments point to an active circulating

00:01:40.863 --> 00:01:41.883
factor instead.

00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:47.203
Worms kept at cooler conditions produced the factor and displayed delayed signs of cellular

00:01:47.203 --> 00:01:50.583
aging, compared with siblings held at standard temperatures.

00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:55.503
measures, one measured outcome was preservation of mobility and tissue integrity over time.

00:01:56.043 --> 00:01:59.463
That effect was large enough to be visible without specialized equipment.

00:02:00.103 --> 00:02:04.983
Muscle is the largest tissue mass in the body and constantly senses and responds to temperature

00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:08.243
changes during routine activity or environmental shifts.

00:02:08.923 --> 00:02:13.303
The next result that would clarify practical relevance is whether the same or a related

00:02:13.303 --> 00:02:16.683
factor appears in human blood after controlled cold exposure.

00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:21.463
A further question is whether it's levels track with any functional aging measures.

00:02:22.272 --> 00:02:27.992
A 2008 study in Cell outlined how declining NAD Plus reduces Sertuan activity.

00:02:28.452 --> 00:02:35.072
That drop alters histone modifications and erodes epigenetic stability, leading to loss of cellular identity.

00:02:35.592 --> 00:02:41.692
The pathway connects falling NAD Plus levels directly to broader cellular aging through these successive steps.

00:02:41.692 --> 00:02:47.232
Researchers identified Sertunans as the link between metabolic state and chromatin maintenance.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:52.472
The work established a framework for viewing aging as progressive information loss at the

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.732
epigenetic level, rather than simple damage accumulation.

00:02:56.532 --> 00:03:01.912
The model positions Sertunans as central regulators that translate metabolic signals into chromatin

00:03:01.912 --> 00:03:02.712
level control.

00:03:03.751 --> 00:03:08.651
Scientists at Ruhr University Bocom and partner institutions engineered light-sensitive

00:03:08.651 --> 00:03:15.371
proteins that suppress activity in targeted cells, in work described on Fizz.org. The tools

00:03:15.371 --> 00:03:20.571
were tested in neurons and cardiac muscle cells to study conditions where excitation inhibition

00:03:20.571 --> 00:03:26.291
balance is disrupted. They offer a way to probe arrhythmias and related disorders with precise

00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:32.431
temporal control. The approach builds on existing optogenetic methods but adds stronger inhibitory

00:03:32.431 --> 00:03:38.291
capacity. The proteins allow researchers to turn down cellular firing or contraction on demand.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.771
using specific wavelengths of light.

00:03:41.371 --> 00:03:44.831
Collaboration across Gottingen, Berlin, Paris, and Essen

00:03:44.831 --> 00:03:47.791
contributed to the design and validation steps.

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:52.679
An insect-borne virus that causes high mortality in white-tailed deer

00:03:52.679 --> 00:03:54.699
has stayed uncommon in New York State.

00:03:55.319 --> 00:03:57.919
The infection mimics foot and mouth disease in cattle.

00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:00.959
Warming conditions could increase the insect vectors

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:02.459
and therefore future spread.

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:06.219
The disease has not yet produced sustained outbreaks in the region.

00:04:06.219 --> 00:04:13.299
The virus affects both wild deer populations and domestic cattle, raising concerns for agricultural surveillance.

00:04:13.899 --> 00:04:18.539
Current data show only sporadic detections despite ongoing ecological surveys.

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:26.189
Exam board materials for secondary science courses in the United Kingdom contain almost no references to female researchers.

00:04:26.929 --> 00:04:32.229
University of Cambridge analysis found that absence in current specifications across multiple boards.

00:04:32.229 --> 00:04:37.709
The gap correlates with higher dropout rates among girls and STEM subjects at age 16.

00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:44.949
The review covered syllabi used for national examinations and identified a near total lack of named women contributors.

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:50.689
Authors suggest the pattern contributes to persistent underrepresentation in later STEM pathways.

00:04:51.309 --> 00:04:56.329
This omission occurs at a critical age when students decide whether to continue in science subjects.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:05:02.525
Candida Auras shifted from an unknown yeast to a widespread health care threat within a few years.

00:05:03.065 --> 00:05:08.565
University of Wordsburg researchers compiled findings from roughly 180 studies on the pathogen.

00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:14.525
The review covers mechanisms of virulence, antifungal resistance, and environmental persistence.

00:05:15.205 --> 00:05:18.865
Authors highlight gaps in understanding its sudden success as a pathogen.

00:05:19.525 --> 00:05:25.345
The organism now appears in hospitals across multiple continents and resists many standard antifungal drugs.

00:05:25.345 --> 00:05:30.185
The summary draws together data on how the yeast survives on surfaces and spreads

00:05:30.185 --> 00:05:35.420
between patients. McGill University tracked how Montreal residents responded to

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.520
environment and climate change Canada advisories during intense smoke events.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.400
Movement patterns shifted less than expected given the health messaging. The

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.400
analysis used travel data collected during Canada's worst wildfire smoke

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.240
episodes. Outdoor activity decreased only slightly even on days when officials

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:58.540
people to stay indoors. The research matched advisory periods with mobile phone

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.780
location records to quantify the actual behavioral response.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:06.320
Authors conclude that additional strategies may be needed to encourage protective

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:11.076
behavior. Rattlesnakes differ in how readily they release venom when threatened.

00:06:11.576 --> 00:06:15.976
Some animals rely more on freezing or rattling, while others escalate faster

00:06:15.976 --> 00:06:20.036
to striking. The variation was documented across multiple encounters

00:06:20.036 --> 00:06:25.976
and natural settings. Observations took place in field conditions where snakes encountered potential threats.

00:06:26.536 --> 00:06:32.276
The study recorded whether each animal chose to remain still, produce warning sounds or inject venom.

00:06:32.896 --> 00:06:35.636
Venom use is not uniform even within a species.

00:06:36.739 --> 00:06:42.439
Banka Island has a big eyeed venomous primate absent from scientific records since the 1930s.

00:06:42.979 --> 00:06:46.819
The animals were found living in gardens, road sides, and near power lines.

00:06:46.819 --> 00:06:46.959
locations.

00:06:47.259 --> 00:06:51.859
Local residents have been contacting a wildlife rescue center after repeated sightings.

00:06:52.379 --> 00:06:56.019
The animal's presence in human-modified habitats surprised researchers.

00:06:56.819 --> 00:07:01.719
Sightings occurred in both rural and more developed areas, prompting rescue calls from people

00:07:01.719 --> 00:07:04.319
who encountered the animals near homes and infrastructure.

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:09.399
The species had not appeared in published literature for nearly 100 years before these

00:07:09.399 --> 00:07:10.419
recent observations.

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:16.877
Facilis Calmet Guran or BCG vaccination can induce trained immunity with broader effects

00:07:16.877 --> 00:07:21.317
on immune function, according to genetic engineering and biotechnology news.

00:07:21.897 --> 00:07:26.437
Researchers are examining whether this trained state reduces dementia risk in older adults.

00:07:27.037 --> 00:07:31.677
The connection builds on known non-specific benefits of the vaccine beyond tuberculosis

00:07:31.677 --> 00:07:32.217
protection.

00:07:32.897 --> 00:07:37.317
The vaccine appears to reprogram innate immune cells so they respond more effectively

00:07:37.317 --> 00:07:38.457
to later challenges.

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:45.277
This non-specific training may extend to protection against neurodegenerative processes that involve chronic inflammation.

00:07:46.057 --> 00:07:49.457
Ongoing studies aim to clarify the mechanism and duration of effect.

00:07:50.527 --> 00:07:56.607
A patient in Abu Dhabi received gene therapy that ended decades of transfusion dependence caused by thalassemia.

00:07:57.127 --> 00:08:02.147
The treatment corrected the underlying genetic defect in blood stem cells, according to Gulf News.

00:08:02.747 --> 00:08:05.867
Follow-up confirms sustained production of healthy hemoglobin.

00:08:05.867 --> 00:08:11.127
The individual had required regular blood transfusions for many years prior to the intervention.

00:08:11.747 --> 00:08:16.267
Post-treatment monitoring showed stable hemoglobin levels without further transfusions.

00:08:16.807 --> 00:08:21.627
The outcome adds to documented successes of in-vivo gene correction for inherited blood

00:08:21.627 --> 00:08:22.147
disorders.

00:08:23.189 --> 00:08:28.469
Vilnius University researchers built perovskite-based lasers that showed no measurable degradation

00:08:28.469 --> 00:08:30.189
after extended operation.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:33.009
In results described on Fizz.org.

00:08:33.009 --> 00:08:37.689
testing use continuous high-repetition rate pumping to simulate real-world

00:08:37.689 --> 00:08:41.909
conditions. The structures were evaluated under conditions that replicate the

00:08:41.909 --> 00:08:46.589
demands of potential device applications. No drop in performance was recorded

00:08:46.589 --> 00:08:51.069
even after hundreds of millions of light pulses. The devices maintained output

00:08:51.069 --> 00:08:55.989
across more than 400 million pulses. The stability addresses a key barrier to

00:08:55.989 --> 00:09:01.250
practical use of the material class. In brief, the Indian Institute of Technology

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:08.350
Madras, or IIT Madras, launched UDO OG, a finishing school that combines three months of online

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:13.350
coursework with four weeks of hands-on training at the Institute's bio-foundry for pre-final

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.490
and final year biotechnology students.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:20.910
Before we go, further surveys are planned to assess population size for the primate now

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.270
turning up in gardens and along road sides on Banka Island.

